1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,730
Variable frame rate in. Constant out?

2
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:16,040
Does it add pictures? Change the length?

3
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:23,210
93 frames over 5 seconds.

4
00:00:23,210 --> 00:00:37,540
Gaps: 33 ms, 67 ms, and one of 933 ms.

5
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:47,510
ffmpeg 6.1.1: 150 frames, 57 duplicates.

6
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:59,150
ffmpeg 8.1.2: 93 frames, uneven gaps kept.

7
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:07,530
-fps_mode passthrough: 93 frames.

8
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:22,200
-fps_mode cfr -r 30: about 150 frames.

9
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:31,170
93 distinct pictures in every variant.

10
00:01:31,170 --> 00:01:41,630
Two counters agree. Still about 5 seconds.

11
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:49,970
60 fps: 207 duplicates of 300 frames.

12
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:57,120
Not tested: any editor or player.

13
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:02,780
Say what you want: passthrough or cfr.

14
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:08,440
Not tested: phone files, editors, other builds.
